K325T stage 3: MiSTer-devel/Minimig-AGA_MiSTer 68EC020 in cpu_wrapper (the TG68K side only)
Transplanted from master 7d5d3c2: c55ecd9 (#276 "Cycle exact 68EC020 (A1200 speed)": cpu_cycles.v
throttle, 32-bit chip cycles w32/r32/c_long, chip_din2/chip_dout2), 09226f7 (68EC020 instruction
cache and chip-bus fetch), f1af4fe (no chip-bus read where TG68K skips the fetch), cf24493, 897af79
(memory ready last in the CPU enable).  The 68030/MMU, CDTV, A2065, RTG and Action Replay parts are
not taken (tied off).  K325T keeps: ramsel = autoconfigured Zorro RAM only (now also gated by the
throttle), the autoconfig, the fast-RAM handshake.  cpucfg is 5 bits as in MiSTer (b2 = stock speed);
cachecfg[0] switches the instruction cache with the 68EC020.  The fx68k branch of the mux and the
fx68k instance are unchanged (chip_long / chip_din2 = 0 there).  Declarations of the FSM registers and
ramsel_i are moved before their first use (Vivado).
